{
  "title": "File Upload Security: Antivirus Scanning and Temporary Files | Orchard Core",
  "description": "A file that a user uploads is untrusted input, so it needs checking before it is stored.\n\nAn upload that calls FileCreationService reaches its handlers, and a handler such as the ClamAV Antivirus Scanner can reject the file before it is stored. Files that Orchard Core writes for a short time get their paths from ITempDirectoryProvider, in one tenant-scoped location that you configure.\n\nIn this video:\n• How the upload pipeline checks a file before it is stored\n• What the ClamAV Antivirus Scanner decides, and how to configure it\n• Enabling the scanner, then uploading a clean file, a test file and a file while the scanner is stopped\n• Running the pipeline and writing a handler in your own module\n• Where temporary files go, and how to move them",
